{
  "name": "What to Expect in a Custom Framing Consultation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about getting something custom framed? That first consultation is where all the magic starts! It’s really just a friendly chat to figure out what you’re looking for. Usually, we'll begin by asking you about the piece you want framed. What is it? Where do you plan to hang it? Knowing where it’ll live helps us get a feel for the overall style and atmosphere we need to match. We’ll dive into your preferences for style, talk about different glass and glazing choices (there are so many options to protect your artwork!), and go over matting selections. Don’t worry if you’re not sure about all the technical terms; that’s what we’re here for! We’ll show you samples and even mock up some ideas so you can visualize how it’ll look. After we’ve nailed down the design, we’ll take precise measurements of your artwork and confirm all the details with you. This step is super important to avoid any mistakes down the road. We’ll also give you a clear idea of the price and the estimated turnaround time, which can vary depending on the materials and complexity. The whole goal is to make sure you feel confident and excited about your custom frame. If your piece is particularly valuable, oversized, or just plain tricky, a professional consultation is absolutely key to getting it done right and keeping your artwork safe.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
